NOTES      COLLISION IS IMPOSSIBLE BY CONSTRUCTION, not by convention. RUNID is a pure function of (arch, arm, seed); every path a run writes is RUNID-prefixed, INCLUDING the CLS round-2 pool, because CLS.py:16 derives it from source_root alone. Under released code every arm collapses onto Dataset/Source/HKU-IS_iteration2/ and each run rmtree's the previous run's pseudo-label pool (CLS.py:19-23) -- which is also why patch P0 was required before any arm could be built.
           ROUND-2 PARITY IS PROVED, NOT SAMPLED. CLS appends images as .png (CLS.py:156, via the .jpg->.png rename at Dataloader.py:141-142), so round 2 trains on a MIXED-EXTENSION pool that no prior experiment ever checked. SrcDataset pairs image to mask by sorted-list INDEX, not by name (Dataloader.py:14-17,29-37), and filter_files is not a pairing guard -- it checks only equal lengths and drops positional pairs whose sizes differ, so a mis-pairing between two images of equal dimensions passes silently. Parity is therefore asserted on the union of each pool with ALL 4040 target names; sorted order is preserved under deletion of the same stems from both lists, and CLS writes image and GT together or skips both (CLS.py:151,155-156), so the union case proves every possible subset.
           WS5' PRE-FLIGHT, ADDITIVE AND STANDALONE (rebuild/REBUTTAL/PREREGISTRATION_WS5.md). Arms B, C10, CSHUF; SINet only; fresh seeds. NEVER POOLED WITH SE, whose verdicts stand untouched. B redraws per seed with default_rng(700000 + seed); C10 and CSHUF are the committed deterministic selections (CSHUF perm_seed 910004). This block TRAINS NOTHING.
           The pools gate checks render masks and B-vs-C overlap for THIS campaign's own B draws (abc_preflight.gate_pools follows the run set's seeds, 2026-11-07).
           VACUOUS BY CONSTRUCTION: "pool content is identical across the two architectures" passes with an empty comparison set, because WS5' builds SINet only. The C-family identical-across-seeds check is non-vacuous and covers all 34 seeds, whatever its label says.
